.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt ICONV 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm iconv
.Nd convert between supported character sets
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl f Ar from
.Fl t Ar to
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility converts the complete input from
.Ar from
to
.Ar to .
The supported sets are UTF-8, ASCII and ISO-8859-1; the accepted aliases are listed in
.Pa docs/posix/P4-locale.md .
With no file operand, or with
.Ar - ,
input is read from standard input.
Output goes to standard output unless
.Fl o
names a file.
.Pp
Conversion is whole-input and produces no partial output on failure.
A character that is not
representable in the target set is an error; there is no transliteration.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for an unsupported encoding or conversion failure, 2 for usage.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gencat 1 ,
.Xr locale 1
.Sh STANDARDS
A documented subset of POSIX
.Nm iconv .
UTF-16, UTF-32, EUC, Shift-JIS, ISO-2022, stateful encodings,
.Fl c ,
.Fl s
and the
.Ql //TRANSLIT
and
.Ql //IGNORE
suffixes are unsupported.
